---
import InstallSteps from "@components/InstallSteps.astro";
---

<section
  id="install"
  aria-labelledby="install-title"
  class="mx-auto mb-16 max-w-3xl scroll-mt-24 px-4 lg:mb-24"
>
  <h2
    id="install-title"
    class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-white md:text-3xl"
  >
    How to install a rEFInd theme
  </h2>
  <p class="mb-8 mt-2 text-pretty text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
    Every theme in the collection installs the same way: copy it into rEFInd's
    <code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1.5 text-sm dark:bg-gray-800"
      >themes</code
    > folder and include it from <code
      class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1.5 text-sm dark:bg-gray-800"
      >refind.conf</code
    >.
  </p>

  <InstallSteps />

  <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
    <strong class="font-medium text-gray-900 dark:text-white"
      >Where is refind.conf?</strong
    >
    On Linux it's usually <code
      class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1.5 dark:bg-gray-800"
      >/boot/efi/EFI/refind/refind.conf</code
    >. On macOS and Windows, mount the EFI System Partition first; open the help
    dialog (<span aria-hidden="true">?</span> in the header) for every path.
  </p>
</section>
